  "factor_name": "Beta-neutral 5-day reversal gated by high cross-asset dispersion",
  "version": "1.0",
  "calculation": {
    "expression": "shift(1, where(mean_cross_asset_20d_realized_vol > rolling_quantile(mean_cross_asset_20d_realized_vol,120,0.60), -[return_5d - beta_60 * benchmark_return_5d] / annualized_volatility_40))",
    "description": "For each tradable asset, remove its 60-day rolling beta exposure to the equal-weight cross-asset benchmark from its 5-day return, then take the volatility-scaled contrarian signal. Activate only when the 20-day average cross-sectional realized volatility is above its trailing 120-day 60th percentile. The one-day shift prevents look-ahead. Positive values indicate expected reversal upside."
